 and  exploration a chore and this is  compounded when you venture into dust an  area of the map enveloped in a thick  poisonous miasma the greatest rewards  can be found in dust but an oxygen meter  controls how long you can stay there for  all the other games in game currency  kuben can be used for an oxygen boost  you can only do this a few times before  it becomes prohibitively expensive  visibility is also reduced and the map  becomes unreliable so it's easy to lose  track of your objective  cause of all this your time in dust  becomes brief and your spoils are often  feel paltry survive zombie like  Wanderers are usually found in isolated  numbers that are easy to pick off by  simply running up behind them and using  an insta-kill attack their movements are  slow and each one behaves exactly the  same combat as a whole is similarly  lacking in dynamism swinging a weapon  and landing a hit feels satisfying and  range combat provides a little more  freedom of movement but overall it's  more functional than fun  in order to actually craft new weapons  and equipment you need to find recipes  for them in containers around dust there  isn't a way of locating containers  outside of randomly stumbling upon them  and it's a crapshoot as to what you'll  get when you find one if you find the  recipe for a new weapon you'll need to  have the relevant materials to craft  them the more exciting stuff requires  rarer materials which are often hard to  come by if you really want or need an  iron your only option is to keep going  back to dust for short stints in hopes  of finding what you need survive does  make exploration and little easier using  wormhole transporters which serve as  fast travel points however powering  these up for the first time draws waves  of Wanderers to your location to fight  off these moments are when Metal Gear  celeb actually feels thrilling to play  and surprisingly it's because of the  limitations of the game systems that  they are setting up before the ambush  you're acutely aware of how little you  have to work with taking our enemies is  tense partly because of how inelegant  movement and attacking fields you need  to be measured and precise to make each  swing count all the while keeping an eye  on your vitals it's a delicate balancing  act in which the stress comes from  knowing how much you've committed to the  battle and the tension is in how much  you stand to lose  [Music]  base-building is also a big part of  Metal Gear Solid's gameplay and there's  enjoyment in spending time and resources  transforming your ramshackle base into  one outfitted with water tanks areas to  grow vegetables and rare livestock  cooking stations and crafting benches  growing your base is perhaps the most  rewarding part of mell get survive but  the game barely explains mechanics such  as resource sharing and creating  exploration teams and crafting and  building evolve navigating a litany of  menus you can also play survive in  online multiplayer during which you team  up with friends in wave based survival  missions equipment and items are shared  between campaign and multiplayer and  this mode is considerably more generous  about doling out materials and weapons  as rewards this is a good way of making  things a little more manageable but  relying on a separate mode to make the  campaign feel manageable feels like an  obvious sign that the single-player  experience isn't balanced properly for  the most part Metal Gear survivor feels  oppressive demonic and obtuse  it's a shame because there's actually a  good survival game in there but the  pressures it places on you makes  uncovering and enjoying that unappealing  over time the ability to balance thirst  and hunger becomes slightly more  manageable especially if you play the  more you player but the lead-up to that  is debilitating there's some  satisfaction to be had by persevering  and savoring the enjoyment of small  victories but you'll quickly find  yourself thinking if your time would be  better spent playing something else  entirely  until you remember what pain is
 

